menu "System Power Management Options"
    config SYS_POWER_TASK_STACK_SIZE
        int "Power Manager Task Stack Size (bytes)"
        default 4096
        range 2048 16384
        help
          Stack of the power manager task (source detection, budget,
          battery estimate).

    config SYS_POWER_TASK_PRIO
        int "Power Manager Task Priority"
        default 4
        range 1 24
        help
          Priority of the power manager task.

    config SYS_POWER_TASK_PERIOD_MS
        int "Power Manager Period (ms)"
        default 1000
        range 100 10000
        help
          How often the manager measures the input, re-detects the source and
          updates the budget and battery estimate. Settings changes wake it
          immediately.

    config SYS_POWER_MAX_CONSUMERS
        int "Maximum Budgeted Rails"
        default 4
        range 1 16
        help
          Most vreg rails a board description can list under the budget.

    config SYS_POWER_BUDGET_STEP_MW
        int "Budget Change Threshold (mW)"
        default 250
        range 0 10000
        help
          The automatic rail caps are recomputed when the budget changes by at
          least this much, so measurement noise on the input voltage doesn't
          reprogram the regulators every period.

    config SYS_POWER_INPUT_WARNING_PCT
        int "Input Current Warning (% of source limit)"
        default 90
        range 10 99
        help
          The input monitor's warning alert is set at this share of the
          source's current limit; the critical alert is at the limit itself.

    config SYS_POWER_BATTERY_HYSTERESIS_PCT
        int "Battery Threshold Hysteresis (%)"
        default 3
        range 1 20
        help
          A battery low/critical event is raised once and re-armed only when
          the charge rises this far above the threshold.
endmenu
